# Micro Workflows - Team Patterns

## Adding a New Feature (Full Stack)
1. Define types in `features/{name}/types/index.ts`
2. Create API functions in `features/{name}/api/index.ts`
3. Build components in `features/{name}/components/`
4. Add translations to ALL 3 locale files (en, fr, ar)
5. Create/update backend endpoint if needed

## Adding a New API Endpoint
1. Add Zod validator in `validators/`
2. Create controller function in `controllers/`
3. Register route in `routes/index.ts`
4. Use `successResponse()` / `errorResponse()` helpers

## Database Changes
- Add new fields as optional first, migrate data, then make required
- Always add indexes for frequently queried fields
- Use `timestamps: true` on all Mongoose schemas

## Error Handling Pattern
```typescript
// Frontend - always show user-friendly messages
try {
  const result = await api.create(data)
  if (!result.success) throw new Error(result.error)
  toast({ title: t('success.created') })
} catch (error) {
  toast({ title: t('error.createFailed'), variant: 'destructive' })
}

// Backend - always return structured errors
if (!validation.success) {
  return errorResponse(validation.error.message, 400)
}
```

## Status Flow for Entities
`pending` → `active` ↔ `inactive` → `archived`

Never delete data - always soft-delete by setting status to `archived`.
